# Billy B-Assistant Deep Dive

This file documents how Billy works end-to-end, with an emphasis on:
- where LLM work happens (provider-side)
- where tool/function logic runs locally on the Pi
- how audio, motors, sessions, and user state interact

## TL;DR: Is everything offloaded to OpenAI?

No.

- The realtime model (OpenAI or xAI) handles speech generation, response text, and deciding whether to call tools.
- Tool implementations are mostly local Python code on the Pi.
- Local handlers can call external services (Home Assistant API, RSS/weather/sports feeds, camera capture commands), then feed results back into the realtime session.
- With xAI, provider-native tools (`web_search`, `x_search`) also execute provider-side.

So the model is remote, but a meaningful part of behavior is local orchestration + local tool execution.

## Main Runtime Architecture

Entry point:
- `main.py` ensures `.env` exists, loads environment, starts MQTT, starts motor watchdog, and enters button/session loop.

High-level components:
- Session orchestration: `core/session_manager.py`
- Session state machine: `core/session/state_machine.py`
- Tool routing/execution: `core/session/function_handler.py`
- Tool definitions and mode filtering: `core/base_tools.py`, `core/session/tool_manager.py`
- Realtime provider abstraction: `core/realtime_ai_provider.py`
- Providers: `core/providers/openai_provider.py`, `core/providers/xai_provider.py`
- Audio I/O and playback/motor sync: `core/audio.py`, `core/session/audio_handler.py`, `core/session/mic_manager_wrapper.py`
- Motor control: `core/movements.py`
- User/persona context: `core/profile_manager.py`, `core/persona_manager.py`, `core/session/user_handler.py`, `core/session/persona_handler.py`
- Triggers and control plane: `core/button.py`, `core/mqtt.py`, `core/say.py`
- Wake-word: `core/wakeword_listener.py` + provider backends
- Web config/API: `webconfig/`

## Startup and Session Lifecycle

1) Boot/start:
- `main.py` loads config and starts:
  - MQTT thread (`start_mqtt`)
  - motor watchdog (`start_motor_watchdog`)
  - button loop (`core.button.start_loop`)

2) Session start triggers:
- Hardware button/wake-word trigger in `core/button.py`
- MQTT command/listen trigger in `core/mqtt.py`
- MQTT say/song flows in `core/mqtt.py` + `core/say.py`

3) Session initialization (`BillySession.start`):
- Reload persona from current user profile.
- Build instructions with user/persona context.
- Build tool list based on guest/user mode and feature flags.
- Connect provider websocket and send `session.update`.
- Optionally inject kickoff message for MQTT say flow.

4) Streaming loop (`BillySession.run_stream`):
- Receives realtime events (`response.created`, transcript deltas, audio deltas, function-call args, `response.done`, errors).
- Routes each event into state/audio/tool handlers.
- Manages mic open/close and follow-up windows.

5) Session end:
- Mic stops, websocket closes, motors/state return idle.
- User interaction count increments.

## Realtime Provider Layer

Provider selection:
- Registered in `core/providers/__init__.py`.
- Default chosen from env keys and `REALTIME_AI_PROVIDER`.

OpenAI path:
- `core/providers/openai_provider.py`
- Websocket: `wss://api.openai.com/v1/realtime?model=...`
- Session config includes instructions, tools, server VAD params, and audio I/O config.
- Provider-specific tools: none.

xAI path:
- `core/providers/xai_provider.py`
- Websocket: `wss://api.x.ai/v1/realtime`
- Similar session setup with xAI fields.
- Provider-specific tools enabled: `web_search`, `x_search`.

Key point:
- Both providers receive instructions + tool schema.
- The model decides if/when to call tools.

## Local Tool-Call Execution (Core Answer)

Tool schema exposure:
- Base tools defined in `core/base_tools.py`.
- User-only tools appended when mode is `user`.
- `ToolManager` filters tools by mode and feature availability (conversation_state toggle, camera hardware).

Function call handling:
- Realtime function-call deltas are buffered in `BillySession._on_tool_args_delta`.
- On `response.function_call_arguments.done`, `FunctionHandler.handle(...)` dispatches local handlers.

Local handlers in `core/session/function_handler.py`:
- `conversation_state` (internal follow-up signal)
- `update_personality` (writes persona traits)
- `play_song`
- `smart_home_command` (Home Assistant call)
- `identify_user`
- `store_memory`
- `manage_profile`
- `switch_persona`
- `get_news_digest` (local fetch/aggregation path)
- `describe_scene` (camera capture + image injection; OpenAI path required in current build)

How result returns to model:
- Handler sends `conversation.item.create` with `function_call_output`.
- Often injects a follow-up user message containing structured context/result.
- Triggers `response.create` so the model speaks a natural answer.

This is why Billy is not "just offloading everything": model reasoning is remote, but tool side-effects and integrations are local.

## Turn Management and Follow-Up Policy

State machine (`core/session/state_machine.py`) tracks:
- assistant/user turn gating
- transcript/audio deltas
- speech/noise heuristics
- follow-up expectations
- retry budget for empty/noisy turns

Follow-up decision path (`core/session_manager.py`):
- Honors explicit `conversation_state` tool when present.
- Falls back to heuristic (question-mark detection) when missing.
- Supports modes: `always`, `never`, `auto`.
- Distinguishes announcement-style sessions vs interactive sessions.
- Reopens mic when follow-up expected; otherwise ends session.

Noise handling:
- Uses chunk count, RMS, loud chunk ratio, server-VAD signals to filter non-speech turns.
- Can cancel short/noisy turns and keep listening without consuming full retries.

## Audio + Motor Pipeline

Input:
- Mic stream captured via `sounddevice`.
- Chunks are resampled when needed and sent as `input_audio_buffer.append`.
- Server VAD events (`speech_started`, `speech_stopped`, `committed`) feed state logic.

Output:
- Realtime audio deltas decoded from base64 and queued for playback.
- Playback worker streams audio to output device.
- Mouth flaps driven by chunk energy while speaking.
- Tail/head movement coordinated during speech and songs.

State signaling:
- MQTT state topic publishes `idle`, `listening`, `speaking`.
- Head retract delay and movement timing managed by state + motor modules.

## User, Persona, and Memory Flow

Instruction context:
- `get_instructions_with_user_context()` builds dynamic prompt from:
  - guest vs user mode
  - active persona instructions/traits/backstory
  - current user profile context

Persistence:
- User profiles and memories live in profile storage managed by `profile_manager`.
- Persona assets/config loaded by `persona_manager`.

Runtime updates:
- `identify_user` can move from guest to known-user context.
- Persona switches can happen mid-session and trigger session updates.

## Trigger Surfaces and External Control

Button:
- Primary local UX for start/interrupt/stop behavior.

Wake-word:
- Optional always-on listener (backend pluggable, porcupine included).
- Paused during active sessions to avoid mic contention.

MQTT:
- Remote commands (`billy/command`) for control operations.
- `billy/say` supports:
  - literal one-shot TTS
  - conversational kickoff mode
  - optional interactive follow-up behavior
- `billy/song` triggers song playback path.

Web UI/API (`webconfig/`):
- Settings, service control, logs, audio tests, motor tests
- Persona/profile CRUD + import/export
- Song management
- News source management
- Camera/wake-word/system routes

## Configuration Surface (Important Knobs)

Provider/model:
- `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_MODEL`
- `XAI_API_KEY`
- `REALTIME_AI_PROVIDER`

Conversation behavior:
- `TURN_EAGERNESS` + `SERVER_VAD_PARAMS`
- `MIC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`
- `SILENCE_THRESHOLD`
- `FOLLOW_UP_RETRY_LIMIT`
- `RUN_MODE`, `TEXT_ONLY_MODE`

Hardware/profile:
- `BILLY_MODEL`, `BILLY_PINS`
- `CAMERA_HARDWARE` and camera capture vars
- wake-word vars (`WAKE_WORD_*`)

Transport/integrations:
- MQTT vars (`MQTT_*`)
- Home Assistant vars (`HA_*`)

## Practical Debug Map

If Billy talks but tools do nothing:
- Check tool appears in session tools (mode/feature flags may filter it).
- Confirm `response.function_call_arguments.done` arrives.
- Verify matching handler exists in `FunctionHandler.handlers`.

If model ignores follow-up behavior:
- Check whether `conversation_state` is enabled for the model.
- Inspect fallback heuristic path for question detection.

If mic appears "stuck":
- Check wake-word listener pause/resume and session lock states.
- Check playback gate/event and mic timeout logic.

If camera tool fails:
- Current scene tool path expects OpenAI provider for Realtime image flow.
- Validate camera hardware setting and capture command dependencies.

## Extension Points

Add new local tool:
1. Add schema in `core/base_tools.py` (or user tool list).
2. Add handler mapping + implementation in `core/session/function_handler.py`.
3. If tool availability should depend on mode/hardware, update `tool_manager`.
4. Ensure handler sends `function_call_output` and triggers follow-up response when needed.

Add new provider:
1. Implement `RealtimeAIProvider` subclass.
2. Register in `core/providers/__init__.py`.
3. Map env/config defaults and provider-specific tools if any.

Add wake-word backend:
1. Implement wake-word provider interface.
2. Register backend in provider registry.
3. Configure via `WAKE_WORD_BACKEND`.

## Bottom Line

Billy is a hybrid architecture:
- remote realtime model for speech + reasoning + tool decisioning
- local orchestrator for sessions/audio/motors/state
- local tool execution for integrations and side-effects

It is not pure OpenAI offload; the Pi runs substantial application logic.
